---
export const title = 'Heading level and narrow widths';
export const order = 200;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  A header inside a section of the page takes another level with <code>heading-level</code>
  (1 to 6). The header responds to its own width, not the viewport's: in a container narrower than
  600px the actions wrap onto their own row under the title and the headline steps down a size.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <div style='width: 100%; max-width: 360px; border: 1px solid var(--color-outline-variant); border-radius: 1rem;'>
    <wc-page-header
      headline='Team members'
      heading-level='2'
      supporting-text='12 people'
    >
      <wc-button slot='actions' variant='outlined'>Export</wc-button>
      <wc-button slot='actions'>Invite</wc-button>
    </wc-page-header>
  </div>
</DemoComponentCard>
